From 71a8f9fa1e0012dc068bd97fb5cf2ddaa93715e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:06:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 4: Control keyboard routing/RTL/parent-changed + Form
 legacy surface

Adds the Control and Form extensibility members custom controls and ported
dialogs rely on. Because they live on Control, they become present on every
derived control, cutting the overall net48 member gap by ~1265 (9787 -> 8522).

Control (Control.Extensibility.cs):
- Keyboard-command routing chain: ProcessCmdKey(ref Message, Keys),
  ProcessDialogKey, ProcessDialogChar, ProcessMnemonic, ProcessKeyPreview,
  ProcessKeyEventArgs, ProcessKeyMessage, IsInputKey, IsInputChar. The chain
  forwards to the parent and raises OnKeyDown/OnKeyPress/OnKeyUp from a key
  message, matching WinForms.
- RtlTranslateAlignment (3 overloads), RtlTranslateHorizontal, RtlTranslateLeftRight,
  RtlTranslateContent - flip left/right under RightToLeft.Yes.
- OnParentBackColorChanged and the rest of the OnParentXxxChanged family (9),
  each raising the matching OnXxxChanged.

Form:
- ProcessCmdKey is wired to real key presses: the form key handler maps the GTK
  key (+Ctrl/Alt/Shift) to a WinForms Keys value via GdkToKeys and routes it
  through ProcessCmdKey before the accept/cancel handling, so form-level shortcut
  overrides fire.
- Legacy lifecycle (Form.Legacy.cs): Closing/Closed/Activated/Deactivate events
  with their On* raisers. Closing/Closed are raised from OnFormClosing/OnFormClosed
  with cancel propagation; Activated/Deactivate are wired to window focus in/out.
- Owned-form management (AddOwnedForm/RemoveOwnedForm/OwnedForms), ParentForm,
  Validate()/ValidateChildren(+ValidationConstraints), CenterToScreen/CenterToParent.

Full suite green at 2315 (+4 tests: RTL flips, ProcessKeyMessage raises OnKeyDown,
ProcessCmdKey parent chaining, legacy Closing/Closed with cancel propagation,
owned forms/ParentForm/Validate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
